# benchmark/longmemeval — runtime knobs (copy to .env or export before run.py).
# EVERYTHING here is selectable. Models are just today's recommendation; the
# world keeps moving, so pass whatever current frontier model matches the
# convention when you run. NOTHING is hardcoded.

# ── models (both optional; empty = gateway default) ──────────────────────────
# ANSWER model = the memory-augmented QA model. Mid-tier is fine + cheap.
#   Recommendation as of 2024/2025: a gpt-4o-mini-class model. Override freely.
DINOMEM_BENCH_ANSWER_MODEL=

# JUDGE model = grades hypothesis vs gold. For a LEADERBOARD-CANONICAL number,
# the convention is a frontier-class judge (gpt-4o was the paper's reference,
# >97% agreement w/ human experts). A weaker judge = directional, not citable.
# Use whatever current frontier model matches the convention when you run.
DINOMEM_BENCH_JUDGE_MODEL=

# ── neuron overlay (arm=neuron ONLY) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The command that lays the neuron overlay onto the already-base-populated lab
# WS. {ws} = lab workspace dir, {lab} = sandbox root (run.py substitutes both).
# --no-auto-base is REQUIRED for arm fairness: base is already laid down, so the
# overlay must NOT re-refresh base from GitHub mid-run (breaks isolation +
# protocol-hash reproducibility). --agree = non-interactive license (AI install).
# --no-cron = ephemeral lab, don't register crons.
DINOMEM_BENCH_OVERLAY_CMD=bash /root/.openclaw/workspace-analyst/github/dinomem-neuron/scripts/install.sh --workspace {ws} --agent-id analyst --agree --no-cron --no-auto-base

# ── optional: custom recall command the answer loop shells (rag/neuron arms) ──
# Leave empty to use the arm's auto-wired default.
DINOMEM_BENCH_RECALL_CMD=

# ── the installed dinomem workspace (source of procedures/tools) ──────────────
DINOMEM_WORKSPACE=/root/.openclaw/workspace-analyst
